<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Literacy Explorer</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #862633;
            color: #333;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #862633;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            font-size: 2.2em;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #ffc72c;
            padding-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .section {
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            border: 2px solid #862633;
            border-radius: 10px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .section-header {
            background: #862633;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px 20px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            font-weight: bold;
            position: relative;
        }

        .section-header:hover {
            background: #ffc72c;
            color: #862633;
        }

        .section-header::after {
            content: "▼ Click to explore";
            position: absolute;
            right: 20px;
            font-size: 0.9em;
            font-weight: normal;
        }

        .section-content {
            padding: 20px;
            background: #f9f9f9;
            display: none;
        }

        .terms-container {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
            gap: 15px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .term-box {
            background: white;
            border: 3px solid #862633;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 15px;
        }

        .term-box:nth-child(even) {
            border-color: #ffc72c;
        }

        .term-title {
            color: #862633;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.1em;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .term-definition {
            color: #555;
            font-size: 0.95em;
        }

        .highlight-box {
            background: #ffc72c;
            color: #862633;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .tip-box {
            background: #862633;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            position: relative;
        }

        .tip-box::before {
            content: "💡 ";
            font-size: 1.2em;
        }

        .instructions {
            background: #e8f4f8;
            border-left: 4px solid #ffc72c;
            padding: 15px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #862633;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>🤖 AI Literacy Explorer</h1>
        
        <div class="instructions">
            📋 Instructions: Click on each section header below to explore AI literacy concepts. Each section contains important information for understanding AI in education.
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection('intro')">
                What is Generative AI?
            </div>
            <div class="section-content" id="intro">
                <p><strong>Generative AI (GenAI)</strong> systems create brand-new text, images, audio, code and more by learning patterns from huge datasets—not by copying existing sentences verbatim.</p>
                
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    That's why ChatGPT can draft an email, Stable Diffusion can paint a scene, and ElevenLabs can clone a voice.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection('terms')">
                Key Terms to Master
            </div>
            <div class="section-content" id="terms">
                <div class="terms-container">
                    <div class="term-box">
                        <div class="term-title">🧠 Artificial Intelligence (AI)</div>
                        <div class="term-definition">Computers performing tasks that normally need human intelligence and decision-making capabilities.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="term-box">
                        <div class="term-title">📊 Machine Learning</div>
                        <div class="term-definition">Algorithms that learn patterns from data instead of following pre-written rules from a programmer.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="term-box">
                        <div class="term-title">🔤 Large Language Model (LLM)</div>
                        <div class="term-definition">A giant neural network trained on massive amounts of text data, like GPT-4, that can understand and generate human-like text.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="term-box">
                        <div class="term-title">✍️ Prompt Engineering</div>
                        <div class="term-definition">The art of crafting clear, specific requests so the AI model delivers exactly what you need.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection('why')">
                Why This Matters for Teachers
            </div>
            <div class="section-content" id="why">
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Knowing HOW GenAI works is the key to deeper conversations about useful outputs, bias, privacy and learning goals—exactly what you need to know to appropriately implement AI with your classes.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header" onclick="toggleSection('tip')">
                Essential Teacher Tip
            </div>
            <div class="section-content" id="tip">
                <div class="tip-box">
                    <strong>Remember:</strong> You don't need to be an expert, just have some knowledge and be honest with the kids.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <script>
        function toggleSection(sectionId) {
            var content = document.getElementById(sectionId);
            var header = content.previousElementSibling;
            
            if (content.style.display === "none" || content.style.display === "") {
                content.style.display = "block";
                header.style.background = "#ffc72c";
                header.style.color = "#862633";
                header.innerHTML = header.innerHTML.replace("▼ Click to explore", "▲ Click to collapse");
            } else {
                content.style.display = "none";
                header.style.background = "#862633";
                header.style.color = "white";
                header.innerHTML = header.innerHTML.replace("▲ Click to collapse", "▼ Click to explore");
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
